WEBVTT

00:33.463 --> 00:35.046
[wind whooshing]

00:49.213 --> 00:50.380
[blowing]

00:52.505 --> 00:55.255
[alarm beeping, switches off]

00:56.588 --> 00:58.921
[tent flap unzips]

00:59.005 --> 01:00.171
[groans softly]

01:00.255 --> 01:02.255
[wind whistling]

01:13.796 --> 01:18.546
[dramatic music building]

01:25.630 --> 01:28.755
[woman] Come on, the sun is out.
It's perfect.

01:29.338 --> 01:30.463
Come on, let's go.

01:30.546 --> 01:34.046
- Can you get up, please, please, babe?
- [man] Mm, okay.

01:34.130 --> 01:36.713
[moaning] Oh, babe, your breath.

01:37.796 --> 01:38.880
You love it.

01:38.963 --> 01:40.505
[woman chuckles]

01:40.588 --> 01:42.255
- Wake up.
- Okay.

01:42.338 --> 01:43.171
- Yeah.
- Hm.

01:43.255 --> 01:44.963
- Go away.
- Let's go. Yeah.

01:45.046 --> 01:47.213
- Leave me alone.
- Let's get going, come on.

01:47.296 --> 01:50.255
- [dramatic music continues]
- [wind whistling]

02:02.963 --> 02:05.171
[groans happily]

02:05.921 --> 02:06.838
[laughs]

02:10.130 --> 02:12.588
- [grunts]
- Hey! Easy now.

02:21.588 --> 02:22.838
[wind whooshes]

02:22.921 --> 02:24.963
[woman] Come on, old man. You got this.

02:25.046 --> 02:26.255
[exhales heavily]

02:27.838 --> 02:29.421
[howls]

02:31.255 --> 02:34.380
[howls]

02:34.463 --> 02:36.255
[howl echoing]

02:38.088 --> 02:39.546
[man] Damn, it's getting cold.

02:39.630 --> 02:41.713
[woman] That's just your Aussie ass.

02:41.796 --> 02:42.921
[man laughs]

02:47.213 --> 02:50.588
- You ready to get to the top?
- Not yet, baby.

02:50.671 --> 02:52.088
Let's go. [blows softly]

02:54.338 --> 02:56.296
- [man] Yeah! You got it.
- [woman grunts]

02:59.463 --> 03:00.463
[grunts]

03:05.921 --> 03:07.255
[groans]

03:09.630 --> 03:10.880
[man] No rush.

03:12.588 --> 03:13.588
[groans]

03:13.671 --> 03:14.671
[yells]

03:15.796 --> 03:17.296
[tense music playing]

03:17.380 --> 03:18.380
You're all good.

03:18.463 --> 03:22.630
It's the same goddamn spot every time.
Gonna be here forever.

03:22.713 --> 03:24.296
How can I help you?

03:24.380 --> 03:26.380
[woman panting]

03:26.463 --> 03:27.671
I'm good.

03:28.630 --> 03:31.130
I got this. I can... [breathing heavily]

03:31.213 --> 03:32.505
I can do this.

03:33.213 --> 03:34.630
[man] Just take your time.

03:35.838 --> 03:36.838
[exhales sharply]

03:37.755 --> 03:39.005
[wind whistling]

03:47.921 --> 03:48.921
[grunts]

03:49.796 --> 03:51.213
[breathes deeply]

03:51.713 --> 03:53.213
- [man] Nice.
- [yells]

03:54.130 --> 03:55.296
[yells in frustration]

03:56.421 --> 03:58.505
[tense, percussive music playing]

04:01.421 --> 04:02.380
[sighs]

04:04.963 --> 04:05.963
What?

04:06.463 --> 04:08.046
I reckon we should call it a day.

04:08.130 --> 04:09.796
It's the final pitch, Tommy.

04:09.880 --> 04:11.671
[grunts]

04:13.796 --> 04:14.796
[yells]

04:16.463 --> 04:18.088
[music fades]

04:18.671 --> 04:20.505
It'll still be there
in the morning, I promise.

04:20.588 --> 04:21.880
[thunder rumbles]

04:21.963 --> 04:24.630
Plus, there's a bit of shit weather
coming in. Have a look.

04:24.713 --> 04:26.255
[woman] Just give me one more try.

04:26.338 --> 04:28.796
We can both hit the top
and make tent well within an hour.

04:28.880 --> 04:30.963
I know we can do that.
I want to summit today.

04:31.046 --> 04:33.505
- [Tommy] That is exactly why--
- No, I want to summit today.

04:33.588 --> 04:35.838
That's exactly why
you have a climbing partner,

04:35.921 --> 04:38.546
so that someone can make the call
when one of you loses the plot.

04:39.713 --> 04:43.171
- So I'm making a call. Okay?
- [sighs]

04:43.255 --> 04:45.171
Sash, it's all good.

04:45.255 --> 04:47.630
It was beautiful climbing,
up until where you... [chuckles]

04:47.713 --> 04:49.005
Right until when it wasn't.

04:52.588 --> 04:54.671
[wind whistling]

04:57.296 --> 05:00.255
Just wondering whether we should
take a rain check tomorrow, that's all.

05:00.338 --> 05:02.421
Are you kidding me?
It's just a little weather.

05:02.505 --> 05:04.505
What's... What's going on?

05:05.255 --> 05:06.505
[Tommy] No, just...

05:07.463 --> 05:11.213
I just feel like sometimes
you rush it a little bit, that's all.

05:15.130 --> 05:17.255
[tent flapping loudly]

05:21.838 --> 05:23.171
Anything else?

05:24.921 --> 05:29.171
[sighs] I don't know how many more
of these trips I've got left in me.

05:29.255 --> 05:34.630
Look, don't get me wrong.
I love this. I love us. I love you.

05:34.713 --> 05:36.421
Stop it. You do this every time.

05:36.505 --> 05:39.171
You know, the climb gets tough,
and then all of a sudden,

05:39.255 --> 05:40.546
you start talking like this.

05:40.630 --> 05:42.505
No, I'm just talking about
slowing it down a bit,

05:42.588 --> 05:44.963
not doing so many extreme things.

05:45.046 --> 05:46.671
[softly] Oh my God.

05:51.005 --> 05:52.296
[Tommy] There's an old saying.

05:52.380 --> 05:54.421
Luck is like anything else
you take up the mountain.

05:54.505 --> 05:56.171
Eventually, it's gonna run out.

05:56.255 --> 05:57.880
You serious?

05:59.296 --> 06:03.088
You're gonna tell me your luck
has run out halfway up a mountain?

06:03.171 --> 06:05.046
If my lucky compass is saying I should--

06:05.130 --> 06:07.921
[Sasha] Oh my God.
Just stop with that fucking compass.

06:12.921 --> 06:14.338
[Tommy] I'm sorry, Sash.

06:15.921 --> 06:17.796
I'm just being a bit of a sook.

06:19.338 --> 06:20.421
Come here.

06:20.505 --> 06:22.505
[Tommy groans]

06:24.546 --> 06:26.255
Where does it hurt?

06:27.296 --> 06:28.296
[Tommy] Yeah, right there.

06:28.380 --> 06:30.005
- Right here?
- [Tommy] Yeah.

06:30.088 --> 06:33.380
[Tommy groans] Jesus.

06:34.880 --> 06:37.505
[Sasha] Promise me we'll be back
after the storm's passed.

06:37.588 --> 06:40.880
We'll get going first thing, okay?
I promise not to sleep in.

06:42.255 --> 06:44.630
- Is that a date?
- [Tommy chuckles]

06:44.713 --> 06:46.713
[wind howling]

06:55.796 --> 06:57.380
[rumbling crash]

06:59.880 --> 07:01.088
[loud thudding]

07:01.171 --> 07:04.421
- [foreboding music playing]
- [rubble clattering]

07:04.505 --> 07:07.296
- [Tommy] Get into the wall!
- [Sasha] Okay, okay, okay.

07:08.046 --> 07:09.505
[Tommy] Keep your head down.

07:09.588 --> 07:11.546
[rubble skidding]

07:14.880 --> 07:17.880
Okay. I want us to go down a little bit.

07:17.963 --> 07:20.380
It's a bit safer there
at that ledge, okay?

07:20.463 --> 07:21.546
[Sasha] Okay.

07:25.088 --> 07:26.630
- [Tommy] You all right?
- [Sasha] Yeah.

07:26.713 --> 07:28.255
You can go faster if you want.

07:28.338 --> 07:29.338
- Oh yeah?
- [Tommy] Yeah.

07:29.421 --> 07:30.880
Now you want me to go faster?

07:30.963 --> 07:32.796
- Yeah.
- [Sasha] All right.

07:32.880 --> 07:34.921
[rope whirring]

07:40.838 --> 07:42.088
[Tommy] You safe?

07:44.755 --> 07:46.421
[both groan]

07:46.505 --> 07:47.630
God.

07:47.713 --> 07:49.713
[foreboding music intensifies]

07:53.963 --> 07:54.921
[Tommy] Are you okay?

07:55.005 --> 07:57.171
Tommy! Get down here!

07:57.255 --> 07:58.796
Did you tie a knot for this rap?

07:58.880 --> 08:00.088
Yeah!

08:03.421 --> 08:05.755
[Sasha] Oh shit! Tommy, wait!

08:05.838 --> 08:07.505
- Just give me a sec.
- [crash]

08:07.588 --> 08:10.880
- [Tommy groans, screams]
- [Sasha] Tommy!

08:12.671 --> 08:13.588
No!

08:14.213 --> 08:15.671
Shit. [breathing heavily]

08:18.505 --> 08:20.171
Tommy!

08:24.546 --> 08:26.338
[panting]

08:26.421 --> 08:30.213
- [metal scrapes]
- [Sasha exclaims] Tommy, wake up!

08:30.296 --> 08:32.963
You're dragging us off the mountain!

08:33.046 --> 08:35.171
[rope creaking]

08:37.463 --> 08:38.546
[groans]

08:38.630 --> 08:41.546
I can't hold it any longer!

08:46.088 --> 08:47.338
[whimpers]

08:47.421 --> 08:49.380
[ominous music pulsating]

08:53.046 --> 08:54.338
[Sasha screams]

08:55.880 --> 08:57.171
[body thuds]

08:58.755 --> 09:00.921
- [music fades]
- [breathing raggedly]

09:01.005 --> 09:02.880
- [metal skids]
- [Sasha screams]

09:04.546 --> 09:06.963
[exhales] Oh!

09:09.463 --> 09:12.671
[ethereal music playing]

09:14.130 --> 09:16.630
[groaning]

09:23.463 --> 09:24.796
[cries out]

09:26.421 --> 09:28.421
[panting]

09:52.005 --> 09:53.505
[music fades]

09:54.463 --> 09:57.171
["Boogie Street" by Leonard Cohen
playing on stereo]

10:08.130 --> 10:09.505
["Boogie Street" continues]

10:10.130 --> 10:15.880
♪ And I'm back on Boogie Street ♪

10:25.671 --> 10:27.671
[brakes squeak]

10:28.630 --> 10:30.671
♪ A cigarette ♪

10:32.838 --> 10:35.463
♪ And then it's time to go ♪

10:37.838 --> 10:41.796
♪ I tidied up the kitchenette ♪

10:43.463 --> 10:47.296
♪ I tuned the old banjo ♪

10:49.130 --> 10:54.713
♪ I'm wanted at the traffic jam ♪

10:54.796 --> 10:58.505
♪ They're saving me a seat ♪

11:00.463 --> 11:03.088
♪ I'm what I am ♪

11:04.005 --> 11:09.338
♪ And what I am
Is back on Boogie Street ♪

11:09.421 --> 11:11.671
- [song stops]
- [insects chirping]

11:11.755 --> 11:15.088
[creature calling in distance]

11:33.380 --> 11:35.671
[pensive music playing]

11:41.546 --> 11:44.880
[Tommy] It's just these climbs, man,
the big tough ones. It's just...

11:45.505 --> 11:46.880
Takes a lot of ego, you know?

11:46.963 --> 11:50.005
If you're nice,
I'll share some of my ego with you.

11:52.671 --> 11:53.963
[sighs]

11:58.088 --> 12:01.338
- [music fades]
- [TV playing indistinctly]

12:19.630 --> 12:20.713
[door closes]

12:21.630 --> 12:22.963
- Hey.
- G'day.

12:24.755 --> 12:26.130
You going out alone?

12:27.130 --> 12:28.671
I wouldn't recommend it.

12:30.380 --> 12:32.588
People get lost in these woods
all the time.

12:32.671 --> 12:34.630
And here, they stay lost.

12:35.296 --> 12:37.130
Can you sign in for us?

12:39.505 --> 12:41.255
Just so we know where you're going.

12:41.338 --> 12:43.338
[pen scratching]

12:46.338 --> 12:47.671
[dog barking]

12:51.130 --> 12:53.963
[man 1] Tough luck. Tough luck.
That's yours.

12:54.046 --> 12:55.755
[man 2] That's the good stuff.

12:56.463 --> 12:58.421
That's the good shit, there.

13:00.671 --> 13:03.588
- Is that packed on?
- For you, it's quite packed on.

13:03.671 --> 13:05.713
- Here you go.
- All right, thank you.

13:05.796 --> 13:06.880
Take it easy.

13:09.088 --> 13:09.921
Hello.

13:12.796 --> 13:13.796
Hey.

13:15.880 --> 13:16.921
[laughs softly]

13:23.296 --> 13:24.713
You got everything you need?

13:25.921 --> 13:28.546
- [man 3] Hey.
- [cashier] Look out. Here's trouble.

13:28.630 --> 13:30.671
How's it going, Mel? Ready for some more?

13:30.755 --> 13:33.255
Oh, yeah. It's selling like hotcakes.

13:33.755 --> 13:34.588
Oh.

13:36.046 --> 13:39.463
- Have you tried it?
- Get real. I wouldn't feed that to my dog.

13:39.546 --> 13:41.005
Well, I think your dog's missing out.

13:41.796 --> 13:42.963
[man 1] Excuse me.

13:43.713 --> 13:44.796
Thank you.

13:45.671 --> 13:47.630
Don't you say "excuse me"
where you come from?

13:49.880 --> 13:51.796
Did you not hear me? I said thank you.

13:57.255 --> 14:00.296
[man 2] Where are you heading?
We could be your guides.

14:00.880 --> 14:02.463
We know the place real well.

14:03.005 --> 14:05.671
- I'm okay.
- We're just trying to be nice.

14:05.755 --> 14:07.505
I think she's okay, fellas.

14:08.588 --> 14:10.671
Looks like she got everything she needs.

14:13.963 --> 14:15.963
[exhales loudly]

14:17.088 --> 14:19.171
- [door opening]
- [bell dinging]

14:19.755 --> 14:22.130
Full tank on six.

14:25.046 --> 14:26.505
I'm sorry about that.

14:27.421 --> 14:29.755
I just thought
I should probably have a bit of a word.

14:29.838 --> 14:32.546
Yeah, you didn't need to. It's okay.

14:32.630 --> 14:33.755
Oh, okay.

14:35.005 --> 14:36.046
No worries.

14:37.463 --> 14:40.505
Thanks, Mel. I'll be back in a tick.
I'm just gonna bring the car around.

14:40.588 --> 14:42.630
[Mel] Yeah. Sixty.

14:46.546 --> 14:47.546
Ta.

14:52.963 --> 14:54.755
Can you add this?

14:58.130 --> 15:00.880
[engine idling]

15:11.713 --> 15:13.213
[chatter on radio]

15:13.296 --> 15:14.755
Hi, hello?

15:14.838 --> 15:17.713
Hi. Um, can you...?

15:18.380 --> 15:19.671
- [switches radio off]
- Hey.

15:19.755 --> 15:21.880
I'm trying to get to Grand Isle Narrows.

15:21.963 --> 15:23.213
- Yeah?
- My GPS is out. Yeah.

15:23.296 --> 15:25.255
- You here for the canyon?
- [Sasha] Yeah.

15:26.380 --> 15:27.380
Yeah.

15:29.046 --> 15:31.005
You want the easy way or the hard way?

15:31.088 --> 15:33.380
Just... the best way.

15:33.963 --> 15:37.213
- Okay. So, this is us.
- [Sasha] Mm-hm.

15:37.296 --> 15:38.505
[man] You make this left,

15:38.588 --> 15:40.880
then it's a bit of a dog leg,
then a straight 50Ks.

15:40.963 --> 15:42.380
Okay, that's easy.

15:42.463 --> 15:45.921
[man] Sorry, can I give you my advice?
Completely different.

15:46.005 --> 15:47.630
[chuckles]

15:47.713 --> 15:49.296
Start at Blackstone Bay.

15:49.880 --> 15:50.880
Here.

15:51.380 --> 15:54.921
- You go about nine Ks.
- [Sasha] Mm-hm.

15:55.005 --> 15:59.046
Just before you get to the split break,
you'll find the most amazing camping area.

15:59.130 --> 15:59.963
[Sasha] Okay.

16:00.046 --> 16:02.546
It's a bit of a well-kept secret,
right by the shore.

16:02.630 --> 16:04.880
- Oh, thanks.
- [man] You think you can handle that?

16:06.421 --> 16:07.796
Yeah, I think I can handle it.

16:07.880 --> 16:08.713
- [man] Okay.
- Okay.

16:08.796 --> 16:10.796
You're gonna love it.
The water's unbelievable.

16:10.880 --> 16:13.005
- Okay, great. I really appreciate it.
- [engine starts]

16:13.088 --> 16:15.338
Okay. Just one more thing to think about.

16:16.088 --> 16:19.171
You know... I hope you know what
you're doing, 'cause it can get intense.

16:19.255 --> 16:21.338
- Intense, I know. It's okay.
- [man] Pretty gnarly.

16:21.421 --> 16:22.796
Most people do it in pairs.

16:22.880 --> 16:23.713
[raises window]

16:23.796 --> 16:25.005
- I'm gonna go.
- Oh, okay.

16:25.088 --> 16:27.130
I wasn't suggesting that you and I do--

16:30.171 --> 16:32.171
[slow, dramatic music plays]

16:48.796 --> 16:50.796
[night chirping]

17:08.671 --> 17:11.671
- [vehicle approaching]
- [music playing faintly on stereo]

17:19.046 --> 17:20.630
[dogs barking]

17:25.088 --> 17:27.963
[heavy metal music blaring]

17:29.005 --> 17:30.088
[quietly] Fuck.

17:31.088 --> 17:32.005
[music stops]

17:32.088 --> 17:33.463
[man 1] That's her again.

17:35.463 --> 17:36.921
Do you want a beer, love?

17:38.213 --> 17:39.630
[sinister music playing]

17:40.546 --> 17:42.546
[rifles cock and uncock]

17:44.546 --> 17:46.463
I think she wants to be alone.

17:47.630 --> 17:49.213
[man 2] You string up the little one.

17:51.296 --> 17:53.171
- [dog barks, growls loudly]
- [Sasha] Oh...

17:53.255 --> 17:54.796
[man 2 laughs]

17:54.880 --> 17:57.380
Oi! Hey, easy.

18:08.755 --> 18:13.005
- [man 1] She's trying to get out.
- [man 2] Sorry, no backing out now, love.

18:14.463 --> 18:15.755
I'm talking to you.

18:20.088 --> 18:22.255
[sinister music continues]

18:26.838 --> 18:28.171
[door locks]

18:38.630 --> 18:39.838
[knocking on window]

18:46.963 --> 18:48.963
We're just trying to be nice.

18:51.630 --> 18:52.838
[door handle rattles]

18:54.130 --> 18:55.130
Okay.

19:04.046 --> 19:07.296
[sinister music continues]

19:11.880 --> 19:14.296
- [men laughing]
- [man 1] You're missin' the best bits.

19:14.380 --> 19:16.671
That's what happens
if you stay in the car all day.

19:16.755 --> 19:19.046
- Look at this beautiful thing.
- [man 3] Right.

19:19.130 --> 19:22.046
[man 2] Okay, let's go.
Diesel, Ripper, get in the truck.

19:23.630 --> 19:24.838
[truck doors close]

19:25.713 --> 19:27.713
[trucks drive off]

19:34.421 --> 19:37.171
- [music fades]
- [birds chirping]

19:51.963 --> 19:56.755
[tranquil music playing]

20:06.671 --> 20:08.755
[music turns thrilling]

20:23.921 --> 20:24.755
[Sasha] Ooh!

20:38.546 --> 20:39.546
[grunts]

20:48.005 --> 20:49.130
[yelps]

21:08.171 --> 21:09.005
[grunts]

21:14.921 --> 21:16.421
[music slows]

21:58.921 --> 22:00.088
[grunts]

22:20.588 --> 22:21.880
[creaks softly]

22:27.963 --> 22:30.046
[somber music playing]

22:42.130 --> 22:44.546
[somber music intensifies]

23:10.171 --> 23:13.088
- [insects chirping]
- [creatures calling]

23:13.171 --> 23:14.255
[music fades]

23:58.630 --> 24:01.713
[pensive music playing]

24:14.005 --> 24:16.713
- [loud screech]
- [wings flapping]

24:16.796 --> 24:17.838
[twig snaps]

24:18.838 --> 24:20.838
[ominous music playing]

24:25.380 --> 24:26.713
[soft rustling]

24:54.380 --> 24:55.505
[softly] What?

25:00.130 --> 25:01.255
What the fuck?

25:04.338 --> 25:05.796
Where's my bag?

25:09.921 --> 25:10.921
Fuck.

25:17.421 --> 25:18.505
- [hisses]
- [Sasha gasps]

25:19.255 --> 25:20.546
Fuck! Fuck!

25:22.588 --> 25:23.421
[exhales]

25:24.463 --> 25:27.046
[breathing heavily]

25:28.505 --> 25:29.588
[hisses]

25:34.338 --> 25:37.171
[mysterious music playing]

26:27.088 --> 26:28.880
- [twig snaps]
- [wings flapping]

26:30.421 --> 26:33.130
[music darkens]

26:55.130 --> 26:56.171
Hello?

27:09.088 --> 27:10.505
[water splashes in distance]

27:14.671 --> 27:15.796
Hello?

27:18.713 --> 27:20.380
Ah! Hey!

27:21.005 --> 27:22.130
Hey.

27:22.213 --> 27:23.630
[man] You made it!

27:23.713 --> 27:25.546
It's me, from the gas station.

27:25.630 --> 27:27.588
[Sasha] Yeah, I remember.

27:27.671 --> 27:28.546
I'm Ben.

27:28.630 --> 27:30.296
Sasha, Ben. Nice to meet you.

27:30.380 --> 27:31.588
[Ben] Hi, Sasha.

27:31.671 --> 27:33.588
Hey, Blackstone Bay.

27:33.671 --> 27:36.171
What'd I tell you?
Dumps you right in the brown.

27:36.255 --> 27:38.630
- Mm-hm. Yeah.
- [Ben] You having fun?

27:39.296 --> 27:41.380
Yeah, the runs are great. I just, um...

27:41.463 --> 27:45.088
Something got into my gear last night
and took everything. My phone, my food.

27:45.171 --> 27:48.046
Oh, bloody hell. That's no good.

27:48.130 --> 27:50.296
Your mobile phone bill's
gonna be through the roof.

27:51.421 --> 27:53.880
Yeah, it's the wombats.
They're texting all the time.

27:53.963 --> 27:55.171
They text constantly.

27:55.255 --> 27:57.796
Yeah, that's a little wombat paw
working the key,

27:57.880 --> 27:59.130
in case you hadn't noticed.

27:59.213 --> 28:01.338
[both laughing]

28:02.046 --> 28:05.296
Seriously, though, I'm sorry.
It's a drastic bummer.

28:05.380 --> 28:08.463
I thought I hung it up high enough,
but guess not.

28:08.546 --> 28:10.463
No such thing out here, I'm sorry to say.

28:10.546 --> 28:13.588
Good news is I always pack
twice what I need.

28:14.296 --> 28:16.630
- I'm more than happy to suit you up.
- Really?

28:16.713 --> 28:17.713
Yeah, of course.

28:17.796 --> 28:19.838
That's what you gotta do out here.
You gotta share.

28:19.921 --> 28:22.046
No other way we all stay alive.

28:22.130 --> 28:24.421
Thanks, Ben. That's really great.

28:25.463 --> 28:26.546
You hungry?

28:27.546 --> 28:29.380
- Just kinda looking for that gear.
- Sit down.

28:29.463 --> 28:31.213
- Let me get you some fish.
- I would really--

28:31.296 --> 28:33.421
Please, I insist. Sit down.

28:33.963 --> 28:36.130
- Okay.
- Yeah, just there. Take a seat.

28:36.213 --> 28:38.588
Eat some food, get the gear, and then go.

28:44.171 --> 28:45.296
[grunts]

28:46.838 --> 28:48.630
[Ben] Yeah, here we go.

28:49.713 --> 28:51.505
So you make beef jerky?

28:51.588 --> 28:52.796
Uh, yeah.

28:53.671 --> 28:56.380
Yeah, I make that myself.

28:58.255 --> 28:59.130
Cut it.

28:59.838 --> 29:00.880
Dry it.

29:01.713 --> 29:04.630
Hang it away from the flies
for a few weeks.

29:04.713 --> 29:06.005
Good protein.

29:07.338 --> 29:11.005
It's not bad. I had some last night.
It's actually really good.

29:11.088 --> 29:12.713
- You tried Jenno's?
- Mm-hm.

29:13.546 --> 29:15.421
Why "Jenno's," by the way?

29:15.505 --> 29:17.130
It was my mum's name.

29:18.296 --> 29:19.546
Named it after her.

29:19.630 --> 29:21.505
You named beef jerky after your mom?

29:21.588 --> 29:22.921
Yeah.

29:23.005 --> 29:25.755
Well, she must be really flattered.
[laughing]

29:29.380 --> 29:31.171
Water. Want something to drink?

29:36.505 --> 29:40.380
Ever seen this before?
It's water siphoned from a tree.

29:43.838 --> 29:45.171
Pretty cool, huh?

29:53.796 --> 29:56.505
Don't worry,
I forgot to pack my roofies. [snickers]

29:58.255 --> 30:00.005
Come on, you gotta hydrate.

30:01.588 --> 30:03.630
Yeah, got to hydrate.

30:04.338 --> 30:05.588
Oh yeah.

30:05.671 --> 30:07.796
That usually impresses people.

30:08.796 --> 30:10.213
Yeah, it's impressive.

30:10.296 --> 30:11.296
Right?

30:12.338 --> 30:13.171
Yeah.

30:14.630 --> 30:15.630
Okay, so...

30:17.713 --> 30:19.255
Spend a lot of time out here?

30:19.338 --> 30:22.213
Oh yeah.
Yeah, I practically live out here.

30:22.296 --> 30:26.296
It's like I'm in pain if I don't get out
on the river once or twice a week.

30:27.088 --> 30:29.005
It's almost physical, you know?

30:30.171 --> 30:31.255
That need.

30:32.255 --> 30:33.921
Where in Australia are you from?

30:34.005 --> 30:36.671
Technically, not from Australia.

30:36.755 --> 30:39.088
No, I come from somewhere
far less appealing.

30:39.671 --> 30:42.255
My mum brought me out here
when I was a kid.

30:42.338 --> 30:44.296
Let me guess. Britain?

30:48.046 --> 30:51.546
- Fuck off. I guessed?
- Yeah, you guessed right.

30:52.505 --> 30:54.796
Uh, how long you been kayaking for?

30:55.338 --> 30:56.171
Mm?

30:56.255 --> 30:58.421
Oh, just a while.
I do a little bit of everything.

30:58.505 --> 30:59.338
Ah!

30:59.421 --> 31:01.255
But mostly mountains, right?

31:03.463 --> 31:05.338
So, I already know about you.

31:06.338 --> 31:08.796
Yeah, you know,
the danger makes you feel alive.

31:08.880 --> 31:12.046
Gotta be in the moment, or you may die.
Perfection's the only option.

31:12.130 --> 31:14.588
All that bullshit
they tell people like us.

31:14.671 --> 31:17.255
Personally, I think
your wiring's just messed up.

31:17.338 --> 31:19.671
You can fight your way
through a lot of shit,

31:20.796 --> 31:22.213
but you can't beat your wiring.

31:23.755 --> 31:26.088
Ain't no mountain high enough, right?

31:28.421 --> 31:29.421
Here you go.

31:30.338 --> 31:31.505
I'm done with mountains.

31:32.713 --> 31:34.255
[Ben] That's interesting.

31:35.213 --> 31:36.796
Let me guess.

31:36.880 --> 31:38.421
You broke up,

31:39.505 --> 31:43.546
and your boyfriend got the mountains,
and you got the rivers.

31:43.630 --> 31:45.130
Am I right?

31:49.213 --> 31:50.380
Oh shit.

31:51.255 --> 31:54.046
- I didn't mean to pry, Sasha. I'm so...
- No, it's fine.

31:54.130 --> 31:55.921
[Ben] I was just trying to be funny. I...

31:56.421 --> 31:58.921
That's the cost
of spending so much time alone.

31:59.005 --> 32:02.380
You completely lose the ability
to function in polite society.

32:03.588 --> 32:05.963
I know what that feels like.
That's why I'm out here.

32:06.046 --> 32:06.963
[Ben grunts]

32:07.713 --> 32:09.880
Don't have to playact like a human being.

32:09.963 --> 32:13.921
[laughs] Yeah. Yeah, there's enough noise
in the world, right?

32:14.005 --> 32:15.338
Speaking of noise,

32:15.838 --> 32:18.338
you know who showed up
at my campsite the other night?

32:19.213 --> 32:20.880
Those hunters from the gas station.

32:21.921 --> 32:23.713
They were definitely messing with me.

32:24.255 --> 32:26.130
Yeah, that's a little concerning.

32:26.713 --> 32:27.755
[Sasha] I know.

32:29.380 --> 32:30.755
[Ben] Assholes.

32:31.755 --> 32:32.796
It's fine.

32:33.421 --> 32:36.130
[Ben] You know,
most hunters aren't like that.

32:36.213 --> 32:41.171
The good ones respect the wilderness,
and we make use of what we kill.

32:41.255 --> 32:44.296
It's not about having an excuse
to drink with your buddies.

32:45.046 --> 32:46.713
It's more reverent than that.

32:46.796 --> 32:49.255
- [Sasha] Yeah, they weren't reverent.
- [Ben] No.

32:49.338 --> 32:50.796
They were trying to scare me.

32:50.880 --> 32:53.338
[Ben] Yeah, no, it sounds that way.

32:55.338 --> 32:57.255
You handled them perfectly, though.

32:59.630 --> 33:00.463
What?

33:00.546 --> 33:02.963
You had grit and poise.

33:03.713 --> 33:06.796
Amazing. You didn't give them an inch,

33:06.880 --> 33:09.380
but you didn't give them
an excuse to hurt you either.

33:09.463 --> 33:11.130
I'm... I'm sorry, what are you saying?

33:11.213 --> 33:12.630
[Ben] At the campsite.

33:13.255 --> 33:16.463
No, I was there.
I thought maybe you could use a hand.

33:16.546 --> 33:20.171
A woman alone and all.
Not the case, though, clearly.

33:20.755 --> 33:22.546
[laughing]

33:23.713 --> 33:25.880
Nah, you're special, Sasha.

33:26.505 --> 33:27.880
Just like my mum.

33:29.130 --> 33:31.255
I could sense it the moment we met.

33:31.796 --> 33:34.046
[sinister music playing]

33:34.130 --> 33:36.338
You're not gonna finish your brekkie?

33:36.963 --> 33:39.213
- Would you like me to wrap it up?
- [Sasha] That's okay.

33:39.296 --> 33:41.463
I'm just gonna get out of here.

33:41.546 --> 33:43.213
Hey, Sasha, what?

33:46.713 --> 33:47.963
Right.

33:49.171 --> 33:50.088
Yeah, this.

33:54.880 --> 33:56.630
I just fancied it.

33:56.713 --> 33:58.296
You want it back?

33:58.838 --> 34:01.338
No? Okay.

34:06.546 --> 34:09.005
I should go, Ben. It's time.

34:12.171 --> 34:13.463
[Ben] Don't forget your bag.

34:15.588 --> 34:17.630
[sinister music intensifies]

34:28.421 --> 34:29.255
[stereo beeps]

34:29.338 --> 34:32.588
["Go" by The Chemical Brothers
playing on speaker]

34:37.005 --> 34:40.463
So, I've restocked
your provisions and supplies.

34:41.130 --> 34:44.713
I've kept your phone, but I threw in
a few extras to level the playing field.

34:44.796 --> 34:46.213
You got the right shoes on?

34:48.046 --> 34:49.380
You'll be fine.

34:49.463 --> 34:50.755
So look, it's very simple.

34:50.838 --> 34:53.921
You've got until the very end of this song
to get as far away from me as you can.

34:54.005 --> 34:55.046
Okay?

34:55.130 --> 34:56.130
Okay?

34:56.213 --> 34:57.755
[Sasha breathing shakily]

34:57.838 --> 34:59.046
[Ben] What's the matter?

35:01.380 --> 35:02.921
I thought you liked danger.

35:03.421 --> 35:05.338
♪ Everything gettin' harder to find ♪

35:05.421 --> 35:07.338
♪ Everybody jumpin' out of they mind ♪

35:07.421 --> 35:08.880
♪ Everybody goin' out of they skins ♪

35:08.963 --> 35:09.963
♪ See we get to the end ♪

35:10.046 --> 35:11.671
♪ But that's where we begin
You feel it ... ♪

35:12.296 --> 35:13.546
[screeches menacingly]

35:13.630 --> 35:15.255
♪ Breakin' out and we breakin' the codes ♪

35:15.338 --> 35:16.838
♪ Similar to the Jacques Cousteau ♪

35:16.921 --> 35:19.838
♪ To the depths and you're wet
So your tank explodes, so get it out ♪

35:19.921 --> 35:21.213
♪ Send your body to flight ♪

35:21.296 --> 35:22.921
♪ Everybody got a target tonight... ♪

35:23.005 --> 35:24.796
[song fades]

35:24.880 --> 35:27.171
♪ All you studs and you duds
And you ladies, let's fly ♪

35:27.255 --> 35:28.130
♪ Grip the moment... ♪

35:28.213 --> 35:30.296
[song continues in the distance]

35:30.380 --> 35:31.796
[Sasha panting]

35:34.755 --> 35:35.588
[grunts]

35:35.671 --> 35:36.880
[song continues loudly]

35:38.255 --> 35:40.255
♪ No time to rest ♪

35:40.838 --> 35:42.255
[song continues faintly]

35:46.255 --> 35:48.255
♪ What you hear is not a test ♪

35:48.338 --> 35:51.713
[softly] Yes! Yes! Yes! Yes!

35:51.796 --> 35:53.505
[song continues faintly]

35:55.380 --> 35:56.671
♪ Go! ♪

35:56.755 --> 35:58.755
[song ends]

36:00.838 --> 36:02.880
[ominous music builds]

36:04.005 --> 36:06.588
[intense music playing]

36:07.796 --> 36:09.463
[exclaims fearfully]

36:16.713 --> 36:18.171
[grunting]

36:47.546 --> 36:49.380
[Sasha exclaims, grunts]

36:49.463 --> 36:51.463
[muffled groaning]

36:58.671 --> 36:59.880
[gasps]

37:04.671 --> 37:05.838
[Sasha coughs]

37:20.505 --> 37:21.838
[coughs]

37:25.380 --> 37:27.380
[retches, coughs]

37:37.088 --> 37:38.546
[coughs]

37:38.630 --> 37:40.755
[insects chirping]

37:56.755 --> 37:59.171
[water splashes]

38:02.421 --> 38:04.421
[bleak music playing]

38:34.880 --> 38:36.421
[woman] Yeah, I reckon it was.

38:36.505 --> 38:37.880
[kid 1] I mean, it could've been.

38:37.963 --> 38:40.088
[man] Let's stay focused on the job.

38:46.046 --> 38:47.963
Look at the birds, up there. Check it out.

38:48.046 --> 38:48.880
[kids exclaim]

38:48.963 --> 38:49.921
Hello?

38:50.005 --> 38:53.546
[woman] Hey, I actually reckon
you two are picking this up really well.

38:53.630 --> 38:54.713
Hello?

38:54.796 --> 38:55.963
[kid 1] Go by Dad's cookbook.

38:56.046 --> 38:57.630
[man] I'm gonna knock it out of the park.

38:57.713 --> 38:59.796
- [woman] Oh yeah?
- [kid 2] Yeah, with rancid fish?

38:59.880 --> 39:02.671
[man] You just wait.
I happen to be quite a bush craftsman.

39:02.755 --> 39:04.546
Are you going to catch a platypus?

39:04.630 --> 39:06.713
- [woman] Yeah.
- [kid 2] Yeah.

39:06.796 --> 39:07.713
[man] How cool is this?

39:07.796 --> 39:10.421
[woman] I know.
Look at those beautiful trees.

39:10.505 --> 39:13.088
- [kid 1] Trees, my eye.
- [Ben on video] Hey, Carters.

39:13.171 --> 39:14.963
[Carters] Hi, Ben!

39:15.046 --> 39:16.796
Hey! [laughing]

39:17.963 --> 39:19.838
- [arrow whistles]
- [tree bark clattering]

39:19.921 --> 39:21.921
[Sasha panting]

39:23.171 --> 39:25.171
[foreboding music playing]

39:31.546 --> 39:33.463
[music intensifies]

39:52.588 --> 39:54.380
- [arrow whistles]
- [Sasha gasps]

40:01.213 --> 40:03.046
Fuck. Fuck.

40:03.130 --> 40:04.130
[screams]

40:07.171 --> 40:08.755
[trills, yips]

40:12.005 --> 40:14.005
[panting]

40:28.546 --> 40:29.880
- [arrow whistles]
- [Sasha yells]

40:35.421 --> 40:38.005
[Sasha screaming]

40:41.255 --> 40:43.005
[yells, grunts]

40:44.463 --> 40:47.005
[yelling, screams]

40:47.921 --> 40:50.921
[dark music playing]

40:54.546 --> 40:55.921
[gasping]

41:04.796 --> 41:06.005
[inhales sharply]

41:17.505 --> 41:19.088
[gasps, grunts]

41:43.296 --> 41:45.046
[music turns somber]

41:48.630 --> 41:52.130
- [birds chirping]
- [creatures calling]

41:59.588 --> 42:00.796
[exhales]

42:41.380 --> 42:43.421
[driving, percussive music plays]

42:52.130 --> 42:55.088
[music pulsates intensely]

43:00.755 --> 43:02.421
[Sasha panting]

43:14.671 --> 43:16.671
[music turns eerie]

43:47.588 --> 43:48.921
[grunts]

43:57.880 --> 43:58.880
[grunts]

44:14.338 --> 44:16.338
[somber music plays]

45:02.546 --> 45:03.630
[music fades]

45:06.880 --> 45:08.880
[panting softly]

45:15.546 --> 45:16.755
[exhales sharply]

45:18.213 --> 45:20.713
- [Ben screeches]
- [wings flapping]

45:20.796 --> 45:22.213
[birds calling urgently]

45:22.296 --> 45:24.380
[tense music plays]

45:31.130 --> 45:32.880
[tense, dramatic music plays]

45:56.255 --> 45:57.296
[exclaims]

45:58.463 --> 46:00.421
[low growling]

46:07.546 --> 46:09.213
[screeches like raptor]

46:11.421 --> 46:13.421
[tense, dramatic music continues]

46:28.421 --> 46:29.880
[Ben hoots]

46:37.463 --> 46:38.546
[faint rustle]

46:39.338 --> 46:41.338
[footsteps depart]

46:43.755 --> 46:44.963
[music fades]

46:45.713 --> 46:46.755
[grunts]

46:47.255 --> 46:48.296
[exhales]

47:04.671 --> 47:06.630
[panting]

47:20.463 --> 47:24.171
[breathing heavily]

47:28.838 --> 47:31.671
["Nasty Boy" by Trabant playing distantly]

47:31.755 --> 47:34.338
♪ I'm a nasty little boy ♪

47:34.421 --> 47:36.421
♪ I'm a little useless ♪

47:36.505 --> 47:39.255
- ♪ I'm a useless little toy ♪
- [Ben whoops]

47:39.338 --> 47:43.421
♪ I'm a little useless
I'm a useless little toy ♪

47:43.505 --> 47:44.671
♪ Ow! ♪

47:47.463 --> 47:49.463
[song grows louder]

47:50.713 --> 47:51.963
[Ben cackles]

47:53.963 --> 47:55.546
♪ You're a little crazy ♪

47:55.630 --> 47:57.755
♪ You're a crazy little sexy girl ♪

47:58.671 --> 48:00.546
- ♪ You're a little crazy ♪
- [Ben whoops]

48:00.630 --> 48:03.380
♪ You're a crazy little sexy girl ♪

48:03.463 --> 48:05.588
♪ I can turn you on all night long ♪

48:05.671 --> 48:07.630
♪ I can turn you on all night long ♪

48:07.713 --> 48:10.380
♪ I can turn you on
Wanna be your boy ♪

48:10.463 --> 48:11.713
[music distorts]

48:17.588 --> 48:19.630
[music continues normally]

48:23.046 --> 48:24.880
♪ I'm a little filthy ♪

48:24.963 --> 48:27.046
♪ I'm a filthy little dog ♪

48:27.880 --> 48:29.546
♪ I'm a little filthy ♪

48:29.630 --> 48:32.630
♪ I'm a filthy little horny dog ♪

48:32.713 --> 48:34.338
♪ I can turn you on all night long ♪

48:34.421 --> 48:36.713
♪ I can turn you on all night long ♪

48:36.796 --> 48:39.713
♪ I can turn you on
Wanna be your boy... ♪

48:39.796 --> 48:40.630
[Sasha groans]

48:40.713 --> 48:44.088
♪ ...your nasty, nasty, nasty little boy ♪

48:46.338 --> 48:47.213
♪ I'm your nasty... ♪

48:47.296 --> 48:48.255
[wood cracks]

48:48.338 --> 48:49.546
[screams]

48:49.630 --> 48:50.880
[Sasha yells]

48:50.963 --> 48:53.463
♪ N-n-n-nasty boy ♪

48:53.546 --> 48:54.630
[song fades]

48:56.005 --> 48:57.255
[trap creaks]

48:58.005 --> 48:59.005
[groaning]

49:03.296 --> 49:05.130
[Ben yips, cackles]

49:11.171 --> 49:12.088
[Ben growls]

49:14.005 --> 49:15.546
[Sasha moaning]

49:17.380 --> 49:19.546
- [Ben yells]
- [bear spray spraying]

49:19.630 --> 49:21.088
[Ben shouting]

49:23.130 --> 49:24.755
[menacing music plays]

49:26.380 --> 49:27.880
- [Ben exclaims]
- [Sasha whimpers]

49:31.046 --> 49:32.713
[coughs]

49:37.796 --> 49:38.755
[Ben yells]

49:39.880 --> 49:41.421
[Ben laughs maniacally]

49:43.713 --> 49:45.463
[Ben grunts] Uh-uh-uh-uh!

49:45.546 --> 49:47.130
[Ben laughs]

49:48.088 --> 49:50.463
[Ben groaning]

49:50.546 --> 49:52.005
Oh, you got me.

49:52.671 --> 49:54.213
Toss the pepper spray.

49:54.296 --> 49:55.880
[menacing music continues]

49:57.088 --> 49:58.255
Okay.

49:59.171 --> 50:02.546
Okay, yeah. Okay, let's get this off you.

50:03.505 --> 50:04.880
On your tummy.

50:04.963 --> 50:07.588
It's okay. It's gonna be okay.

50:07.671 --> 50:09.796
Let's get this off you. Eyes forward.

50:12.296 --> 50:13.880
[Sasha groans]

50:13.963 --> 50:15.213
- [trap snaps shut]
- [Ben] Oh!

50:17.046 --> 50:18.088
Okay.

50:21.838 --> 50:22.921
Oh...

50:26.671 --> 50:27.755
Are you playing a game?

50:32.671 --> 50:35.671
Is that what you think we're doing?
You think we're playing a game, Ben?

50:35.755 --> 50:37.046
[Ben] It's not a game.

50:38.088 --> 50:39.588
It's a ritual.

50:39.671 --> 50:41.671
[foreboding music playing]

50:44.671 --> 50:48.880
- [rope creaking]
- [Sasha grunting]

50:52.255 --> 50:54.255
[music continues]

51:22.713 --> 51:24.546
[Ben] Hey! Hey, hey, don't.

51:47.671 --> 51:48.921
[music fades]

51:51.046 --> 51:52.380
You don't like being tied up?

51:54.046 --> 51:56.505
There's something
seriously wrong with you.

51:57.921 --> 51:59.130
[Sasha sighs]

52:05.505 --> 52:07.505
Now, come on, I gave you a choice.

52:08.838 --> 52:10.963
"You want the easy way or the hard way?"

52:12.713 --> 52:14.755
What did you choose? [ grunts]

52:14.838 --> 52:16.588
[Sasha groans softly] Mm.

52:16.671 --> 52:19.130
Let me know
when you reach your pain threshold.

52:19.213 --> 52:20.546
[Sasha groans]

52:21.296 --> 52:23.546
Don't disappoint me, Sasha.

52:25.838 --> 52:28.338
- [menacing music builds]
- [Sasha breathing deeply]

52:37.880 --> 52:39.880
[dark music playing]

52:51.963 --> 52:54.046
Rituals are very important.

52:55.046 --> 52:56.421
They ground us.

52:57.671 --> 52:59.755
They remind us of who we are.

53:03.921 --> 53:06.755
Did you know there are tribes
that file down their own teeth

53:06.838 --> 53:08.005
to sharp points?

53:10.296 --> 53:11.296
Hm?

53:12.880 --> 53:16.005
Enduring pain is a part
of growing up, Sasha.

53:17.296 --> 53:19.255
It's a rite of passage.

53:24.296 --> 53:26.296
[music intensifies]

53:42.671 --> 53:44.171
[music fades]

53:44.838 --> 53:46.255
Where are we going, Ben?

53:48.296 --> 53:49.630
I'll tell you later.

53:53.380 --> 53:56.380
You don't want to explain
the rules to me this time?

53:58.630 --> 54:02.213
I got your name from the ranger's register
and did a bit of a search.

54:05.421 --> 54:07.088
So the Troll Wall...

54:09.796 --> 54:11.963
I guess you don't wanna talk about that.

54:17.380 --> 54:19.630
It was just an unfortunate accident.

54:20.338 --> 54:23.380
Yeah, but I read online
that he was really experienced.

54:24.046 --> 54:27.963
He made some gnarly summits.
Doesn't really make sense.

54:28.630 --> 54:30.421
Things can always happen.

54:31.421 --> 54:34.088
[Ben] Yeah, I guess
nobody gets it right every time.

54:34.755 --> 54:37.630
I think it's the mental challenge
you gotta be ready for.

54:38.463 --> 54:40.505
You gotta be mentally prepared.

54:41.088 --> 54:43.130
That's it. I think you're right, Ben.

54:43.213 --> 54:46.171
- [Ben] Yeah.
- [Sasha] I absolutely agree with you.

54:47.088 --> 54:48.921
It's all in your mind, right?

54:49.005 --> 54:51.713
- Yeah, it's all in the mind, right?
- Yeah.

54:52.755 --> 54:54.796
What about the funeral.
Was it hot or cold?

54:58.588 --> 55:00.171
He was cremated.

55:00.255 --> 55:02.463
So did you come here to scatter his ashes?

55:03.046 --> 55:06.171
You're bringing the Aussie home.
He was from around here, right?

55:06.671 --> 55:09.130
[tense music plays]

55:15.171 --> 55:16.588
- [Sasha yells]
- [Ben laughs]

55:17.880 --> 55:20.296
Okay. [laughing]

55:23.296 --> 55:26.505
Uh-uh-uh! Stay there. Stay there.

55:27.213 --> 55:28.296
[gasps sharply]

55:31.963 --> 55:34.130
[grunts, whoops exuberantly]

55:34.755 --> 55:36.130
[Sasha gasps]

55:36.713 --> 55:38.338
[tense music continues]

55:46.588 --> 55:47.921
[inhales sharply]

55:54.963 --> 55:56.921
[music slows]

55:58.463 --> 56:01.046
[muffled groaning]

56:01.630 --> 56:03.296
[gasping]

56:07.921 --> 56:09.963
[panting]

56:22.505 --> 56:23.796
[music fades]

56:23.880 --> 56:26.421
[birdsong]

56:42.463 --> 56:43.505
Why?

56:45.255 --> 56:46.796
So you can get down there.

56:48.463 --> 56:50.005
[Ben taps harness] Put it on.

56:51.505 --> 56:53.463
[ominous music playing]

56:57.171 --> 57:00.213
- [water dripping]
- [harness creaking]

57:30.713 --> 57:35.421
[unsettling music playing]

57:39.963 --> 57:41.505
[Sasha gags, groans]

57:52.213 --> 57:54.421
[ominous sting]

58:01.213 --> 58:02.130
[Sasha gasps]

58:02.963 --> 58:05.880
There are native tribes that say

58:05.963 --> 58:09.921
to capture the spirit of your prey,
you have to consume its liver.

58:10.546 --> 58:13.713
The trick is finding a spirit
worth capturing, I suppose.

58:16.338 --> 58:18.755
You remember the Carters from the video?

58:20.046 --> 58:22.213
They didn't put up much of a fight.

58:23.296 --> 58:24.921
Not like you.

58:26.088 --> 58:29.546
I try to take as much care
and attention as possible.

58:32.546 --> 58:34.713
At the end of the day,
they're all human beings.

58:35.296 --> 58:37.921
And it's important
to make use of the kill.

58:39.171 --> 58:40.921
Every part of it.

58:41.505 --> 58:42.838
Nothing goes to waste.

58:44.713 --> 58:46.255
[Sasha breathing sharply]

58:47.880 --> 58:49.630
[Ben] It's more reverent that way.

58:50.380 --> 58:51.421
Am I right?

58:52.005 --> 58:53.713
Oh my! [groans]

58:53.796 --> 58:58.088
- Oh my God. No!
- You must be exhausted from the journey.

58:58.171 --> 59:00.796
- No, no, no! [whimpering]
- [Ben] Why don't you take a rest?

59:00.880 --> 59:02.963
Come on, yeah, it's okay.

59:03.046 --> 59:05.380
- [Sasha] No!
- Come on, come to my bedroom.

59:06.463 --> 59:07.463
Yeah.

59:08.671 --> 59:09.921
Yeah.

59:10.005 --> 59:11.046
[Sasha groans]

59:11.130 --> 59:13.046
[Ben, sighing] Oh!

59:13.630 --> 59:17.005
[Sasha exclaims, breathing heavily]

59:20.380 --> 59:22.088
Hey, can I ask you something?

59:25.338 --> 59:27.713
[softly] You really think
I've got a problem?

59:29.796 --> 59:31.796
[unsettling music playing]

59:38.005 --> 59:39.005
I think...

59:41.380 --> 59:43.505
I think people hurt you.

59:45.713 --> 59:47.796
And they did bad things to you.

59:49.463 --> 59:50.463
Uh...

59:52.796 --> 59:56.046
And I'm so sorry
those things happened to you, Ben.

59:56.130 --> 59:57.755
- I can't imagine what...
- [Ben sighs]

01:00:06.755 --> 01:00:07.880
[Ben groans]

01:00:16.671 --> 01:00:18.421
[breath trembles]

01:00:30.255 --> 01:00:32.380
[chain rattles]

01:00:45.046 --> 01:00:46.213
[Sasha] Please, stop.

01:00:50.755 --> 01:00:51.838
[tense sting plays]

01:00:55.796 --> 01:00:57.796
[breathing shakily]

01:01:10.088 --> 01:01:11.088
Ben?

01:01:15.671 --> 01:01:16.671
Ben?

01:01:20.546 --> 01:01:21.546
[Ben screeches]

01:01:21.630 --> 01:01:23.505
- [ominous music playing]
- Oh, no!

01:01:23.588 --> 01:01:25.338
- No! No!
- [Ben snarling]

01:01:26.963 --> 01:01:28.921
[both grunting]

01:01:56.630 --> 01:01:58.296
Do you know what this is?

01:01:59.546 --> 01:02:00.380
Hm?

01:02:01.213 --> 01:02:04.046
This is my homemade salt brine.

01:02:04.130 --> 01:02:05.671
[liquid sloshes]

01:02:05.755 --> 01:02:08.296
It's a perfect tenderizer.

01:02:08.963 --> 01:02:11.588
It's a very important part of the process.

01:02:18.338 --> 01:02:20.380
The photo next to your bed?

01:02:23.505 --> 01:02:25.046
Is that your mom?

01:02:26.588 --> 01:02:28.755
She looks just like you.

01:02:33.713 --> 01:02:34.838
Yeah.

01:02:46.380 --> 01:02:49.505
[Sasha breathing heavily]

01:02:49.588 --> 01:02:52.005
[softly] Do you know
what she used to say to me?

01:02:56.421 --> 01:02:59.296
"Jenno loves Benno."

01:03:01.755 --> 01:03:04.088
"And Benno loves Jenno."

01:03:04.171 --> 01:03:06.005
- [Sasha laughs awkwardly]
- Yeah.

01:03:10.755 --> 01:03:12.338
She was special.

01:03:14.046 --> 01:03:16.505
She was the first one.

01:03:25.463 --> 01:03:26.921
Do you understand?

01:03:30.046 --> 01:03:32.255
Now she's always with me.

01:03:36.338 --> 01:03:38.296
I'm gonna keep you with me too.

01:03:43.546 --> 01:03:45.088
[Sasha] You're a sick fuck.

01:03:45.171 --> 01:03:46.796
[Ben screams]

01:03:54.838 --> 01:03:56.338
- [Ben grunts]
- [Sasha screams]

01:03:57.380 --> 01:03:59.963
- [fabric rips]
- [Ben grunting]

01:04:01.005 --> 01:04:02.005
[Sasha grunts]

01:04:04.796 --> 01:04:06.088
[Ben] Sasha!

01:04:08.130 --> 01:04:09.755
[Sasha yells]

01:04:12.255 --> 01:04:13.546
[frenetic music playing]

01:04:24.588 --> 01:04:25.630
[Sasha screams]

01:04:26.713 --> 01:04:29.755
[gasping desperately]

01:04:29.838 --> 01:04:31.005
[yells]

01:04:31.796 --> 01:04:33.130
[Ben yells]

01:04:37.255 --> 01:04:41.296
[terrifying music playing]

01:04:45.130 --> 01:04:46.463
[Ben] Sasha!

01:04:47.796 --> 01:04:48.796
Sasha!

01:04:48.880 --> 01:04:50.213
[gasps]

01:04:57.838 --> 01:04:59.255
[Sasha screams]

01:05:07.088 --> 01:05:08.130
[cable creaks]

01:05:24.380 --> 01:05:25.588
[muffled groan]

01:05:32.755 --> 01:05:33.838
[muffled groaning]

01:05:38.630 --> 01:05:40.005
[muffled screams]

01:05:54.630 --> 01:05:57.338
[gasps, panting heavily]

01:06:03.046 --> 01:06:05.130
[tense music playing]

01:06:16.255 --> 01:06:17.421
[Sasha grunts]

01:06:32.296 --> 01:06:33.463
[groans softly]

01:06:35.963 --> 01:06:37.046
[strained grunt]

01:06:40.880 --> 01:06:42.338
[Sasha screams]

01:06:42.421 --> 01:06:43.671
[gasps]

01:06:43.755 --> 01:06:44.671
Fuck.

01:06:44.755 --> 01:06:45.588
[coughs]

01:06:47.130 --> 01:06:49.130
[Sasha yelling]

01:06:52.755 --> 01:06:53.713
[Sasha yells]

01:06:57.463 --> 01:06:59.671
[tense music continues]

01:07:01.796 --> 01:07:03.171
[both grunting desperately]

01:07:03.255 --> 01:07:04.380
[Sasha yells]

01:07:06.463 --> 01:07:07.630
[grunts]

01:07:18.171 --> 01:07:21.421
[both grunting]

01:07:30.880 --> 01:07:32.546
[grunting animalistically]

01:07:41.838 --> 01:07:42.671
[low growling]

01:07:43.421 --> 01:07:44.963
[breathing deeply]

01:07:46.838 --> 01:07:48.338
[gasps]

01:07:49.088 --> 01:07:50.296
[coughs]

01:07:51.838 --> 01:07:52.671
It's okay.

01:07:54.255 --> 01:07:55.088
[Ben groans]

01:07:58.588 --> 01:07:59.713
- [Sasha grunts]
- [Ben screams]

01:07:59.796 --> 01:08:00.713
[bone cracks]

01:08:00.796 --> 01:08:01.630
[Sasha screams]

01:08:01.713 --> 01:08:03.796
[Ben screams]

01:08:08.588 --> 01:08:09.630
[whimpers]

01:08:13.796 --> 01:08:15.963
[Ben groans loudly]

01:08:16.046 --> 01:08:18.838
- [Ben whimpering]
- [uneasy music playing]

01:08:18.921 --> 01:08:21.255
[pained grunting]

01:08:28.713 --> 01:08:32.213
[screams] You've broken my leg!

01:08:33.880 --> 01:08:36.505
[sobbing]

01:08:38.921 --> 01:08:40.171
[Ben screams]

01:08:41.713 --> 01:08:43.963
[Ben continues sobbing]

01:08:44.046 --> 01:08:46.421
[Sasha grunts, exhales]

01:08:47.088 --> 01:08:49.213
[Ben sobbing]

01:08:50.630 --> 01:08:54.463
- [eerie music playing]
- [Ben wailing]

01:09:26.588 --> 01:09:28.463
[mosquito buzzing]

01:09:28.546 --> 01:09:30.546
[Sasha laughs dryly]

01:09:32.838 --> 01:09:35.296
People come here on vacation.

01:09:36.546 --> 01:09:37.463
[laughs]

01:09:41.213 --> 01:09:43.630
You must have one hell of a dentist.

01:09:47.630 --> 01:09:49.463
Or did you eat him too?

01:09:52.546 --> 01:09:53.505
[buzzing stops]

01:09:57.630 --> 01:09:59.171
[thunder rumbles]

01:10:01.296 --> 01:10:03.588
You ever get depressed in the dark?

01:10:10.755 --> 01:10:13.296
Feel like you misjudged things?

01:10:17.838 --> 01:10:19.171
Feel guilty?

01:10:25.671 --> 01:10:27.005
When he fell...

01:10:29.546 --> 01:10:32.338
he was dragging
both of us off the mountain.

01:10:34.546 --> 01:10:36.546
[solemn music plays]

01:10:40.088 --> 01:10:41.630
[softly] I had to let him go.

01:10:49.296 --> 01:10:52.255
I'll never know if he was still alive.

01:10:55.630 --> 01:10:58.588
I was only there because he was there.

01:11:00.380 --> 01:11:02.838
And he didn't want to be there anymore.

01:11:03.713 --> 01:11:04.796
[laughs dryly]

01:11:07.005 --> 01:11:08.755
I didn't listen.

01:11:14.130 --> 01:11:15.880
I just kept pushing.

01:11:23.421 --> 01:11:25.463
[solemn music continues]

01:11:40.880 --> 01:11:42.880
[flies buzzing]

01:11:52.713 --> 01:11:54.296
What's back there, Ben?

01:11:55.630 --> 01:11:57.796
[Ben] About 12 days of walking.

01:11:57.880 --> 01:11:59.546
[Sasha] You'll never survive it.

01:12:00.046 --> 01:12:02.005
Yeah, and whose fault is that?

01:12:03.546 --> 01:12:05.921
I have to get
to the top of that wall today.

01:12:08.505 --> 01:12:10.713
We either get up there today...

01:12:13.296 --> 01:12:15.255
or I wait for you to die.

01:12:16.880 --> 01:12:20.213
And you will. From an infection.

01:12:20.796 --> 01:12:22.505
You can't climb it without me.

01:12:28.213 --> 01:12:29.213
Maybe.

01:12:31.338 --> 01:12:34.963
Maybe you're right. It is a tandem climb.

01:12:35.046 --> 01:12:36.505
Let's do it.

01:12:37.005 --> 01:12:38.630
Come on. Okay?

01:12:40.130 --> 01:12:41.630
Let's do it together.

01:12:45.588 --> 01:12:46.630
It's okay.

01:12:51.963 --> 01:12:54.671
I'm gonna tell you how to tie a knot

01:12:54.755 --> 01:12:57.463
with some of that rope
to make a booster for your good leg.

01:12:58.088 --> 01:13:00.088
And we'll build you a harness.

01:13:00.588 --> 01:13:03.380
A diaper harness.
It's the only way to get you up there.

01:13:03.463 --> 01:13:04.755
I've already got a harness.

01:13:04.838 --> 01:13:08.963
If I'm gonna lead this climb,
I can only do it with that harness.

01:13:13.880 --> 01:13:15.796
You can't do it, Ben.

01:13:17.255 --> 01:13:18.296
[sighs in distress]

01:13:22.130 --> 01:13:24.546
Take these off so I can help you.

01:13:28.963 --> 01:13:31.005
Do it over by the wall, okay?

01:13:35.963 --> 01:13:36.880
[Ben groans]

01:13:37.671 --> 01:13:38.671
Fuck.

01:13:46.046 --> 01:13:47.505
It needs to be tight.

01:13:49.171 --> 01:13:50.171
Tighter.

01:13:53.796 --> 01:13:54.921
Come here.

01:14:01.546 --> 01:14:03.130
Just so you know,

01:14:03.213 --> 01:14:06.421
when you get us to the top,
I'll set you free.

01:14:06.505 --> 01:14:10.546
But if you try to drop me,
then I will rip you off that wall.

01:14:11.588 --> 01:14:13.796
[tense music playing]

01:14:23.088 --> 01:14:25.130
Don't you dare touch this harness.

01:14:34.880 --> 01:14:37.213
[tense music continues]

01:14:37.296 --> 01:14:39.296
[birds cawing]

01:14:45.380 --> 01:14:46.255
[grunts]

01:14:52.421 --> 01:14:54.130
[screams]

01:15:17.671 --> 01:15:19.130
[groans]

01:15:32.921 --> 01:15:34.380
[groans]

01:15:41.546 --> 01:15:42.838
[exhales]

01:15:53.671 --> 01:15:55.088
[grunts]

01:16:20.005 --> 01:16:22.296
- [Ben] Hey!
- [Sasha screams]

01:16:23.713 --> 01:16:26.546
- Fucking idiot!
- I told you not to touch the harness!

01:16:26.630 --> 01:16:28.130
[Ben yells in pain]

01:16:28.213 --> 01:16:31.338
- I was just resetting it.
- Not the fucking leg!

01:16:32.046 --> 01:16:33.921
[Sasha grunts]

01:16:36.380 --> 01:16:38.421
[tense music continues]

01:17:08.255 --> 01:17:09.796
Hey, can I ask you something?

01:17:11.755 --> 01:17:13.005
When Tommy fell,

01:17:13.088 --> 01:17:15.296
did it look like he was flying?

01:17:34.255 --> 01:17:35.338
[groans]

01:17:36.296 --> 01:17:38.921
Yeah! Come on!

01:17:39.963 --> 01:17:42.380
[Sasha grunting, panting]

01:17:48.630 --> 01:17:50.088
Nice. Nice work.

01:17:52.963 --> 01:17:54.630
[whoops]

01:17:55.421 --> 01:17:56.546
Yeah!

01:17:58.755 --> 01:18:00.380
We make a good team, don't we, eh?

01:18:02.046 --> 01:18:03.255
You know what I mean?

01:18:04.963 --> 01:18:06.588
[bird screeches]

01:18:08.171 --> 01:18:10.255
[tense music continues]

01:18:16.005 --> 01:18:17.255
Hey, Sasha?

01:18:18.921 --> 01:18:20.421
[Sasha] All right. You're good.

01:18:23.671 --> 01:18:25.505
[creaks]

01:18:32.463 --> 01:18:33.880
[groans]

01:18:35.380 --> 01:18:36.421
Hey, what've you done?

01:18:37.463 --> 01:18:39.046
- Sasha!
- Ow!

01:18:40.546 --> 01:18:42.963
You promised me we'd do it together!

01:18:43.046 --> 01:18:44.546
[yells furiously]

01:18:44.630 --> 01:18:45.630
No!

01:18:45.713 --> 01:18:47.380
[both yelling]

01:18:48.671 --> 01:18:49.671
[Ben] Don't do it!

01:18:49.755 --> 01:18:51.005
[Sasha whimpering]

01:18:51.088 --> 01:18:53.713
- [Ben roars]
- [Sasha crying out]

01:18:57.338 --> 01:18:59.671
Sasha! [roars]

01:19:04.671 --> 01:19:06.671
[panting]

01:19:17.171 --> 01:19:18.421
[screams]

01:19:22.546 --> 01:19:23.630
[gasps]

01:19:25.921 --> 01:19:26.963
[exhales]

01:19:34.213 --> 01:19:36.838
- [solemn music plays]
- [birds cawing]

01:19:54.380 --> 01:19:56.380
[heartbeat thumping]

01:20:10.380 --> 01:20:11.921
[heartbeat fades]

01:20:12.005 --> 01:20:13.921
[wind whistling]

01:20:17.838 --> 01:20:20.796
[Sasha breathing heavily]

01:20:23.755 --> 01:20:25.838
[somber music plays]

01:20:49.546 --> 01:20:50.380
[softly] Okay.

01:20:53.463 --> 01:20:54.421
[groans]

01:20:56.296 --> 01:20:58.921
[groans, blows air]

01:21:08.088 --> 01:21:09.463
[exhales deeply]

01:21:12.671 --> 01:21:14.671
[music intensifies]

01:21:28.463 --> 01:21:31.171
[groaning softly]

01:21:34.213 --> 01:21:36.046
[screams]

01:21:36.130 --> 01:21:38.630
[yelling]

01:21:38.713 --> 01:21:40.796
[suspenseful music playing]

01:21:48.713 --> 01:21:49.588
[yells]

01:21:56.421 --> 01:21:59.130
[groans] Fuck!

01:22:01.213 --> 01:22:02.963
[panting]

01:22:05.505 --> 01:22:06.505
Okay.

01:22:14.213 --> 01:22:16.213
[dramatic music plays]

01:22:21.046 --> 01:22:22.338
[sighs]

01:22:23.755 --> 01:22:24.921
[groans]

01:22:29.213 --> 01:22:31.338
[breathes deeply]

01:22:41.130 --> 01:22:42.296
[grunts forcefully]

01:22:56.630 --> 01:22:59.380
Okay. [groans]

01:23:10.171 --> 01:23:11.380
[grunts]

01:23:19.505 --> 01:23:21.505
[panting]

01:23:31.421 --> 01:23:33.421
[breathing heavily]

01:23:41.338 --> 01:23:42.505
[moans]

01:23:46.171 --> 01:23:48.130
[panting]

01:23:54.755 --> 01:23:56.838
[laughs]

01:24:09.005 --> 01:24:11.005
[birds chirping]

01:24:14.296 --> 01:24:16.296
[grunts, exhales]

01:24:29.130 --> 01:24:31.255
[sobs softly]

01:24:52.755 --> 01:24:54.796
[water splashing]

01:25:08.713 --> 01:25:10.755
[night chirping]

01:25:14.963 --> 01:25:16.963
[slow, dramatic music plays]

01:25:21.880 --> 01:25:23.921
- [door closes]
- [woman] Are you lost?

01:25:29.463 --> 01:25:31.380
Do you need water or anything? Or...?

01:25:33.213 --> 01:25:36.088
Could you please take me
to my car at Blackstone Bay?

01:25:37.171 --> 01:25:38.546
[woman] Yeah, of course.

01:26:01.463 --> 01:26:02.588
[door closes]

01:26:07.046 --> 01:26:09.380
[somber music playing]

01:26:09.463 --> 01:26:10.921
[ranger] Do you need help?

01:26:13.796 --> 01:26:14.921
Are you okay?

01:26:16.380 --> 01:26:17.880
I know where they are.

01:26:22.171 --> 01:26:23.255
All of them.

01:26:24.171 --> 01:26:25.505
[somber music intensifies]

01:26:26.921 --> 01:26:28.380
[reporter] Authorities have confirmed

01:26:28.463 --> 01:26:30.505
that at least 20 bodies
have been recovered

01:26:30.588 --> 01:26:33.338
from a cave
deep in Wandarra National Park.

01:26:33.421 --> 01:26:36.296
